.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CXREF 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cxref
.Nd print a C cross-reference table
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility scans C source files and prints one cross-reference row per definition:
.Ar name Ns \t Ns Ar kind Ns \t Ns Ar file : Ns Ar line Ns \t Ns Ar refs .
.Ar refs
is a comma-separated list of
.Ar file : Ns Ar line
occurrences, or
.Ar -
when there are none. The definition line is not repeated.
.Pp
Recognized kinds are
.Cm function ,
.Cm global ,
.Cm macro ,
.Cm struct
and
.Cm enum .
References are lexical identifier matches, so a same-named local can appear.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the table to
.Ar file .
.Ar -
writes to standard output.
.It Fl x
Select the cross-reference table; this is the only mode and the default.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a file or output error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cflow 1 ,
.Xr ctags 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm cxref .
Preprocessor evaluation, C++, typedef aliases, struct members, enum constants and the
.Fl c ,
.Fl s ,
.Fl t
and
.Fl u
options are unsupported.
